# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/draft-vocab four-card DEVELOPMENT window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/draft-vocab and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-dvocab-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head (sed -i 's/tp4-dvocab-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# B0 (STOP): the window image, built from the pushed branch head with the SHIP profile baked as the image's serving default (ENV QWEN_C2_PROFILE) and THATCH_SERVING_SESSION_CAP baked as its
# max-num-seqs (8): the SAME default production runs (c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic), so the image could serve. It carries draft_vocab_tp, the named id list and its
# statistics (both copy lists and the overlay), the tau lab's dvocab arm and the two timing twins; the lever is off unless a job's profile turns it on. REFUSED by c2_serving_job.read_bake while the
# profile's owner_traffic_waiver decision is not APPROVED. READ: 'baking the serving default c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic with a session cap of 8', the provenance report with no
# problem line (draft_vocab_tp.py, draft_vocab_coding_40960.ids and .json are in docker/qwen-c2-overlay.txt), the image id. A build, not a card job: it may run while the cards serve, never during a timing
# job. Duration (estimate): 40 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-dvocab-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic
